WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.860
-Here we have Octavia Spencer
and Melissa McCarthy.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.160
I know you guys are best
friends and so we thought

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.877
we'd do a fun game, almost
like a best friends challenge,

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:13.312
just to see how close
you guys are.

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.514
I mean, Octavia,
you guys are close, correct?

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:17.383
-Of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:18.617
-Yeah. All right,

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.653
and so here's the way it works.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.755
It's called "The BFF Showdown."
-Okay.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.757
-I'm going to quiz you to
determine which of you

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.326
knows the most about
the other one.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.294
-Ooh.
-We got this.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.129
-All right?
You think you got this?

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.098
All right, here we go.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.567
If you get a question right,
you get a point.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.669
Okay, here we go.
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.873
Melissa,
the first question is for you.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.507
-Okay!

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:44.744
-Where did Octavia
go to college?

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:50.617
-Uh...

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.752
You know what? I don't think
she went to school.

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:58.190
-I absolutely did go to school.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.794
-Yeah, okay.
I'm getting, like,

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.230
probably like
a Ft. Lauderdale University

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.031
kind of feel.

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:07.967
-Um...
-Lauderdale?

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.903
-Uh, no.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.371
It's an easy one, Melissa.
Auburn! Auburn!

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:13.872
[ Buzzer ]
I went to Auburn.

00:01:13.872 --> 00:01:15.508
-In Lauderdale?

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.976
-Uh, okay. Let's just --

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:20.012
Octavia, this one's easy.
Ready, Octavia?

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:21.647
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.816
-Is Melissa married?

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:28.822
-[ Chuckles ]
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.757
Pass.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.191
-That was
a pretty easy one there.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.961
I mean, you want to
pass on that one?

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:38.731
-You're gonna pass?
-I think I'm going to pass.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:44.103
-What do you mean, like, Ben?

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:47.272
Ben.

00:01:47.272 --> 00:01:49.409
Well, he's not my cousin.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.010
-All right, all right.
Let's just --

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.280
Right now it's 0-0,
so anyone can still win.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.782
-Okay, this is just a fluke.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.051
-So we'll get rid
of that round one.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.318
Now, this will be
the new round one.

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:00.986
Okay, we'll start
and we'll edit that out.

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:04.490
It's -- here we go. Melissa.
-Yes?

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.527
-What is Octavia's last name?

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:10.229
♪♪

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.698
I know, it's easy.
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:16.169
-You know what? It's --
I just don't say it.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.770
You know,
you don't usually say --

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:21.541
It's -- Man, it's like on
the tip of my --

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:27.046
It rhymes with her
first name, I think.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.914
It's not Octavia, isn't it?
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:31.684
-Octavia Octavia?

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.818
Melissa?

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:34.386
-Maybe I'm thinking
of your middle name.

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:37.790
-No, no. It's -- It's --

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.159
It doesn't rhyme.
-Wow.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.962
-No rhyming.
Can we edit all that out

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.565
and, like, let this be
the first question?

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:48.968
-Octavia Boctavia.
Octavia Boctavia.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.103
-I think that you would know
your best friend's last name,

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:52.272
wouldn't you? I mean --

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.973
-Well, I mean, she's right,
you never say it.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.974
[ Laughter ]
You just never say it.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.143
-Nobody -- If you're friends,

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.611
you don't say
the other person's last name.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:02.215
That'd be so creepy.
I don't curtsy to her either.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:05.752
-This next one -- Here we go.
Super easy.

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:08.721
Octavia, what does Melissa
look like?

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.525
Just a hint --
You can see her on Zoom now.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.494
♪♪

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:18.164
-Let's look now.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:23.336
-Okay, um...

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.238
-One of these boxes
on the screen...

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:27.039
-She's wearing green.
-...is Melissa.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.307
[ Buzzer ]
What's that?

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:31.477
-She's wearing green.
-No, you're wearing green.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:34.780
-I'm not wearing Green.
Are you looking at yourself?

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.384
-Oh.
Well, I guess that is me, huh?

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.386
-Uh, okay.
Let's go to the --

00:03:41.386 --> 00:03:42.655
cut to the last question.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:46.058
Okay, this one is worth
a million points.

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:49.061
Usually when we play the game,
it gets harder as we goes on,

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:51.263
but this one I'm going to
make this really easy. Ready?

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.332
-It started hard.
You started hard.

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.735
-Yeah.
-All right, here we go.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.203
This one's very easy.
A million points.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.871
Whoever gets this wins.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:04.710
Either one of you guys say one
thing about the other person.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:09.215
♪♪

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.450
-See, Jimmy --
-Here's the thing, no one --

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.252
you guys have just been silent.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.154
It is -- anyone says anything,

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.689
I'll give you a million points
about the other person.

00:04:17.689 --> 00:04:20.292
-I just -- You know what?

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:22.862
We just need to be transparent.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.097
We don't really like --

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:27.100
we don't really hang out
in real life.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.369
No, we're Hollywood friends.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.605
You know, like, when the camera
stops, we stop.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:36.241
-Wow. Okay, I get it.
I'm sorry. Wow.

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:37.810
-I've never actually
seen her in person.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.913
-Really?
-You know, how you kind of,

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:45.417
it's like, whenever you hire,
you know, the two little,

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:47.420
the two little girls
that play your daughter.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.389
-No, I didn't hire those girls.
That's my actual daughters.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:52.158
They're my kids.
-That sweet woman you got

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.059
playing your wife, I mean,
I really love her.

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:55.895
You guys have good chemistry.
-She is good.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.663
-Yeah.
-She's really good.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:59.765
-She is my wife.
-Almost convinced me.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.300
You almost convinced me.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.703
-She is my wife.
-"My kids are really my kids."

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.738
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:08.741
-Me, too.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.277
-Okay. Well, we'll be right back

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:15.614
with non-friends Octavia Spencer
and Melissa McCarthy.

00:05:15.614 --> 00:05:17.115
When we come back,
more "Tonight Show, everybody."

00:05:17.115 --> 00:05:19.184
-Can I use your kids?

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:21.287
I want to shoot something,

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.922
and I need a couple kids
to play my kids.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.757
-No, they're not actors, though.

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:26.492
That's -- they're just
actual just kids.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.793
-It's okay.
I'll call their agents.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.896
It's fine.
-They don't have agents.

